id: pm-q4avk2
title: macOS registry acceptance rejects empty optional flags under Bash nounset
description: "Release run 35336550780 published 2026.9.18 successfully but macOS npm-local and Bun acceptance failed before invoking the harness: flags[@]: unbound variable. The macOS Bash version rejects expanding an empty array with set -u. Preserve strict shell failure behavior, candidate/control arguments and global mode, and execute the workflow command under a compatible shell regression before advertisement."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-18T11:27:18.367Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-18T11:33:53.603Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-18T11:33:21.954Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-18T11:33:21.954Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-ygli86
resolution: Initialize the optional-argument array with required JSON output; execute actual workflow commands under native Bash for npm local/global and Bun with success and nonzero exit controls.
expected_result: All install modes reach registry acceptance without empty-array nounset failures; failed acceptance commands still fail their job.
actual_result: Bash 3.2 fails npm and Bun before the fix and passes all four workflow tests afterward; 42 related contracts pass. Hosted PR validation and same-tag recovery remain required delivery steps.
