comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T11:27:18.367Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for flags unbound and macOS release acceptance plus open/in-progress inventories found no existing empty-array failure owner. Canonical completed registry acceptance parent pm-ygli86 is retained; this is a newly observed workflow defect with job logs 105581312635 and 105581312654."
  "2026-09-18T11:31:30.841Z","harness:codex","Red-first reproduction: GNU Bash 3.2 built in a temporary directory executes the actual parsed release workflow step. Before the fix, npm-local and Bun fail with flags[@]: unbound variable, while npm-global passes. Initialize flags with the always-required --json argument so expansion is nonempty under nounset; retain set -euo pipefail. The same test now passes all three modes and independently proves npm exit status 37 propagates. Mandatory macOS PR runtime-smoke job runs this test with /bin/bash. GNU upstream documents the empty-array behavior change in Bash 4.4: https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/bug-bash/2019-05/msg00024.html"
  "2026-09-18T11:33:21.295Z","harness:codex","Verification: Bash 3.2 red/green reproduced the exact hosted refusal and validated all install-mode success/failure paths. All 42 release/CI workflow tests pass; focused ESLint, zero duplication and gate-registry checks pass. The native macOS PR gate must pass before merge. After merge, dispatch Release from main for existing v2026.9.18 to re-run exact artifact acceptance and advertisement; the existing public npm version is verify-only."
  "2026-09-18T11:33:53.603Z","harness:codex","Recovery evidence is linked through GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1272 and the Release workflow exact-tag runs. The issue comment will retain the terminal recovery run and publication/advertisement outcome after this reviewed fix lands; this avoids direct-main post-merge tracker writes."
